<title>VIETNAM: Five die in Vietnam cement factory accident.</title>
<headline>Five die in Vietnam cement factory accident.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five men were scorched to death at a cement factory in northern Vietnam when hot chemicals escaped from a blast furnace, an official at the plant said on Friday.</p>
<p>He said an investigation had been launched into what caused Tuesday's accident at the Hai Duong plant, where the men had been trying to unblock lime and clay that had been heated to more than 500 degrees centigrade (932 Fahrenheit).</p>
